{"error":"dsh-wire.selected-source-not-delivered-or-invalid","diagnostic":{"ok":false,"value":{"context_read_ids":["3c67d2ccaab3b79c5b7e6e551bece8dc1f82df40d850290ceac613aeea58f6e7","60245d4e2bf6c736df69c04c24d5ebae03eb26ff7ec9c2ed1f05a82e33b8c3d2","28160ab4f093ffb3d6eb5df1c7f0450f7065baed119716a1dc7909e52a72ffe2","3086c6ba892883aa25c282ae8e8c3ce992b768503f596cde650a46c481a95f9a"],"summary":"Issue #1241: on first use of a compression context, the match window was zero-initialized (dictLimit = lowLimit = 0), making input position/index 0 potentially treated as a valid match/dict reference. Fix: added MEM_STATIC ZSTD_window_init() in lib/compress/zstd_compress_internal.h that initializes the window with base/dictBase pointing to an empty string, dictLimit = lowLimit = 1, and nextSrc = base + 1, so indices start at 1 and position 0 is never valid. Replaced the memset(&ms->window, 0, ...) in ZSTD_reset_matchState (lib/compress/zstd_compress.c) with a call to ZSTD_window_init(). Verified consistency: ZSTD_invalidateMatchState/ZSTD_window_clear then yields lowLimit = dictLimit = nextSrc - base = 1, and the first ZSTD_window_update sets base = ip - 1, keeping the first input byte at index 1."},"issues":[{"instance_path":"/context_read_ids/3","schema_path":"/bindings/base_source_provenance","keyword":"provenance","code":"final-selection.source-integrity-failure","read_id":"3086c6ba892883aa25c282ae8e8c3ce992b768503f596cde650a46c481a95f9a"}],"truncated":false,"category":"source-integrity-failure","instrument_error":true},"projection_errors":[{"read_id":"3086c6ba892883aa25c282ae8e8c3ce992b768503f596cde650a46c481a95f9a","error":"EROFS: read-only file system, mkdtemp '/tmp/are-cb-source-map-XXXXXX'"}],"observed":[{"id":"749dee0f55c2a879b3eb9468abdddf951e49b5058060d481e21011837642c201","path":"contrib/adaptive-compression/adapt.c","tool_call_id":"call_f51cb6a92fd5477cb7ef1f58:search:0"},{"id":"c4c147c7e4b2e94f75a4c55939e623f4d5d2f09099661d1a1e2b019d6cc71787","path":"contrib/exper